# Asset files are data, not source. Git's end-of-line conversion must not touch
# them (Phase TSUSHIMA-I).
#
# glTF is JSON, so git happily treats it as text and rewrites its line endings
# on checkout. The bytes on disk then differ from the bytes the publisher
# served, which makes `tools/fetch_foliage.sh`'s MD5 verification fail forever
# on exactly the file it most wants to verify — and leaves every fresh clone
# with a working tree that reports the model as modified the first time the
# fetch script is run against it.
#
# `-text` disables the conversion in both directions and says nothing about
# whether git may diff the file, which is what we want for a readable JSON
# asset: still diffable, never rewritten.
assets/**/*.gltf -text
assets/**/*.json -text

# Everything binary, marked explicitly rather than left to git's heuristic.
*.bin binary
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
*.exr binary
*.glb binary
*.ktx2 binary
*.dds binary
*.flac binary
*.ogg binary
*.wav binary
*.somcap binary
*.tbmp binary
